  "count_definition": "Actual final executions across O0/O2 and P/E cores, not unique inputs. Query pairs compare complete represented GPRs/flags, segment/system state, active events and RAM; compiled-return checks are subsets. Earlier focused/diagnostic/failed attempts are not added.",
  "native_boundary": "224 functions per profile: both operations, 16/32-bit result and address widths, seven segment-prefix choices and independent live/dead value/ZF outputs. Each runs CPL0/CPL3, 20 selectors, two flag images and eight memory configurations. Original instruction bytes are independently encoded and authenticated. All queries retain native selector reads even with dead results.",
  "fault_observation": "Original #PF/#AC handlers expose their vector through completed OUT. Both restart PCs are authenticated before normalizing only that frame PC. Inactive exception payload is excluded only after proving neither pending nor injected; other event fields remain compared.",
  "cs_address_contract": "The image is loaded at linear 0x10000 with CS.base=0x10000. Function/control-flow RIPs remain within 64 KiB in code16; debug addresses are separately linear. Existing flat helper callers retain their original wrapper and are regressed through ARPL, far-pointer/segment loads and frame/system returns.",
  "negative_controls": "Every final profile rejects zeroed offset transport before an intact native query and an inverted returned ZF after an intact query. Successes/rejections check prior/value/ZF selection, return ESP and callee-saved registers.",
