    "The descriptor-name filter matched no tests in the separate lightweight backend binary. This zero-test result is not counted as coverage; the full ten-test backend suite and three native-address frontend tests were then run and passed.",
    "The first code16 native fixture placed code above 64 KiB with flat CS; a taken compiler branch truncated IP. A nonzero CS base and explicit relative/linear breakpoint coordinates fixed the fixture without changing query code generation.",
    "The next host build diagnosed an unused flat fault-helper wrapper. Making that retained compatibility wrapper inline fixed the -Werror failure.",
    "The first final code32 run passed its O0 native matrix, then the offset negative-control generator could not fit a prefixed word XOR into the compiler dword-copy extent. Zeroing the full 32-bit carrier preserves the intended negative test and fits both modes. Final profiles were rerun after this fix."
  ],
